{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 90,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lord, thou hast been our dwelling-place\nIn all generations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Before the mountains were brought forth,\nOr ever thou hadst formed the earth and the world,\nEven from everlasting to everlasting, thou art God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou turnest man to destruction,\nAnd sayest, Return, ye children of men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For a thousand years in thy sight\nAre but as yesterday when it is past,\nAnd as a watch in the night.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou carriest them away as with a flood; they are as a sleep:\nIn the morning they are like grass which groweth up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the morning it flourisheth, and groweth up;\nIn the evening it is cut down, and withereth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we are consumed in thine anger,\nAnd in thy wrath are we troubled.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast set our iniquities before thee,\nOur secret sins in the light of thy countenance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For all our days are passed away in thy wrath:\nWe bring our years to an end as a sigh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The days of our years are threescore years and ten,\nOr even by reason of strength fourscore years;\nYet is their pride but labor and sorrow;\nFor it is soon gone, and we fly away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who knoweth the power of thine anger,\nAnd thy wrath according to the fear that is due unto thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So teach us to number our days,\nThat we may get us a heart of wisdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Return, O Jehovah; how long?\nAnd let it repent thee concerning thy servants.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh satisfy us in the morning with thy lovingkindness,\nThat we may rejoice and be glad all our days.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Make us glad according to the days wherein thou hast afflicted us,\nAnd the years wherein we have seen evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let thy work appear unto thy servants,\nAnd thy glory upon their children.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.90.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And let the favor of the Lord our God be upon us;\nAnd establish thou the work of our hands upon us;\nYea, the work of our hands establish thou it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ],
  "headings": [
    {
      "style": "ms1",
      "text": "Book IV",
      "before_verse": 1
    },
    {
      "style": "s1",
      "text": "God’s eternity and man’s transitoriness.",
      "before_verse": 1
    },
    {
      "style": "d",
      "text": "A Prayer of Moses the man of God.",
      "before_verse": 1
    }
  ]
}
